```

New route in `routes/products.js`, same pattern as the existing paged list:

```js
router.get("/search", async (req, res) => {
  const q = (req.query.q || "").trim();
  if (!q) return res.json([]);
  const rows = await db.query(
    `SELECT id, sku, name, price_cents,
            ts_rank(search_vector, websearch_to_tsquery('english', $1)) AS rank
     FROM products
     WHERE active AND search_vector @@ websearch_to_tsquery('english', $1)
     ORDER BY rank DESC
     LIMIT 50`,
    [q]
  );
  res.json(rows);
});
```

The two forks that matter: exact/prefix matching (users typing partial SKUs or truncated words) needs `pg_trgm` + trigram GIN index alongside FTS, not instead of it; and typo tolerance is out of scope for `tsvector` — that's the next level down if the roadmap needs it.

